{"name":"Fever Dream","hex":"#dd5577","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fever dream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intense or confusing dream, often caused by fever.","Any intense, vivid and surreal experience.\nAn outlandish and complex subject matter and plotline in media."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fever_dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fever dream","blocks":[{"text":"A fever dream is a type of dream that transpires during fever or febrile illness, when the body experiences a significant elevation in body temperature beyond normal variation. These dreams are known for their bizarre or surreal experiences. While common in children, these dream occurrences can happen to people of any age. Fever dreams also have significant overlap with delirium and hallucinations."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fever_dream","wikidata":"Q123224208"},{"title":"Fever Dream (Of Monsters and Men album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fever Dream is the third studio album by Icelandic band Of Monsters and Men, released on 26 July 2019 through Republic Records. The album was co-produced by the band with Rich Costey, and was preceded by the lead single \"Alligator\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Of_Monsters_and_Men_-_Fever_Dream.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fever_Dream_(Of_Monsters_and_Men_album)","wikidata":"Q65130552"},{"title":"Fever","blocks":[{"text":"Fever or pyrexia in humans is a symptom of an anti-infection defense mechanism that appears with body temperature exceeding the normal range caused by an increase in the body's temperature set point in the hypothalamus. There is no single agreed-upon upper limit for normal temperature: sources use values ranging between 37.2 and 38.3 °C in humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Symptoms-fever.jpg/330px-Symptoms-fever.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fever","wikidata":"Q38933"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/500px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/1280px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg/500px-Virgil_Solis_Febris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Febris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirgil_Solis_Febris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg/500px-Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg/500px-Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Usha Dreaming Aniruddha (oleographic print) Raja Ravi V